Alice Turner: Quick callout — opening a docs PR to tighten up the error-ref for 429 / timeouts / context limits and the recommended fallback flow. Need short, copy-pasteable SDK snippets + a tiny migration note (<150 words). @Ben @Carla can you review?

Ben Cho: On it. Which SDKs do we want? JS + Python?

Carla Nguyen: JS + Python + optionally Go. Keep examples minimal. Also we should standardize the phrasing: 'context trim' vs 'context clip' — pick one and use it everywhere.

Alice Turner: Let's standardize on 'context trim' (matches runtime naming). Plan: 1) tiny JS snippet showing retry-with-backoff + fallback-to-slim-model; 2) python example for detecting 429 vs timeout and invoking fallback; 3) short migration note about honoring Retry-After header. Also one link fix: point /docs/optimizations/batching instead of the old path.

Ben Cho: For JS snippet, propose using the SDK's error shape. e.g.:

```js
// retry + fallback example (minimal)
async function generateWithFallback(client, prompt) {
  try {
    return await client.text.generate({ model: 'redwood-1', prompt });
  } catch (err) {
    if (err.status === 429) {
      // back off then try a lightweight model
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 300));
      return await client.text.generate({ model: 'redwood-1-small', prompt });
    }
    throw err;
  }
}
```

Carla Nguyen: That looks good. Keep comments short so snippet is compact in the rendered docs. Also I'll search/replace 'context clip' -> 'context trim' across the err-ref page.

Jen Patel: Add an explicit note about Retry-After in the migration blurb. A short line: 'Respect Retry-After header before retrying' — many customers currently ignore it.

Mike R.: Also add a tiny QA checklist in PR description so reviewers can validate behaviour: reproduce via stress tool, ensure snippet builds in the example site, check link redirects. I can add the stress command here:

`./tools/stress-send --rate=200 --duration=30s --model=redwood-1`

Carla Nguyen: Where should the 'fallback policy' examples live? On the err-ref page or split into a dedicated /docs/ops/fallback-policies page?

Alice Turner: Keep concrete snippets on the err-ref page (less hopping). Add a short anchor and cross-link to /docs/ops/fallback-policies for policy-level guidance. That avoids duplication.

DocsBot: CI: docs-lint passed for branch `alice/errref-fallbacks`. Linkcheck found 1 redirect: /old-batching -> /docs/optimizations/batching. (details: ci/4567)

Ben Cho: :thumbsup: I'll push a tiny lint fix to the JS snippet (remove trailing comma) and a note to the PR description explaining the Retry-After expectation.

Alice Turner: @Jen can you draft the <150 word migration paragraph? Ping me when pushed. Goal is to ship this afternoon.

Jen Patel: Draft pushed to branch. Excerpt:

"When upgrading clients to newer runtime behavior, ensure your retry loops respect server Retry-After headers, minimize repeated token usage by prioritizing prefix/cache hits, and fallback to lightweight model variants when latency or 429s spike. Test with production-like request rates and use canary routing to limit blast radius during rollouts."

Mike R.: I'll run the stress job and report results. If linkcheck only surfaced a redirect we should update the canonical link in the content before merge.

Carla Nguyen: Pushed the link fixes and a couple of micro-copy edits. I shortened the JS comments so the example renders compactly in the sidebar.

Alice Turner: Thanks — merging once Mike confirms the stress run looks good. If anyone needs to drop final micro-edits, do them in the branch now. :sparkles:

DocsBot: Merged by Alice Turner — PR #789. Staging deploy started (staging/docs/789).

Mike R.: Stress run complete: 200rps for 30s produced ~12% 429s against `redwood-1`; automatic fallback to `redwood-1-small` reduced observed errors to 0. Logs: ci/789-stress. Given that, merging looks safe.
